SUMMARY:Breathwork & Wellness Social: Donation Based
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Lose The Booze Crew (20-40s)\nInterested in learning
  about breathwork? Me too! Let's attend this donation based event at Wunde
 rland\, a new eco-adventure resort that offers a variety of wellness-focus
 ed amenities! See below for details from Wunderland:\n\nJoin us for a 75-m
 inute breathwork experience with local breathwork guide\, Sasha Bannister.
  Active breathwork is a full-body meditation for your heart\, body\, and m
 ind. We'll use breath to move energy\, release stuck tension\, and quiet t
 he mental noise. Expect to leave feeling lighter\, clearer\, and more embo
 died. It's like taking an internal shower.\n\nBreathwork session will be f
 rom 11a-12:15p\, hosted by Sasha Bannister.\nAt 12:20p\, you can enjoy a b
 rief 25-minute talk about circadian health\, from Restorative Health Pract
 itioner\, Leigh Etheridge.\nAt 12:45p\, you may choose to head home\, or s
 tay for an optional community social\, complete with sauna\, cold plunge\,
  and soul trail!\n\nPlease bring water\, and a blanket or yoga mat (and pi
 llow/bolster if you wish). If you choose to stay for the community social 
 after breathwork and circadian health talk\, please also bring a bathing s
 uit and towel as well!\n\n☀️Note: While the event is FREE to attend\, 
 there is a suggested $11 donation.☀️\n\nIf you have any questions abou
 t the event itself\, please contact events@wunderlandresort.com. If you ha
 ve questions about the meetup\, feel free to message me!\n\nHope to see y
 ’all there!🤗
